The PE build links with -flto=thin, with LLVM that finds the symbols inline asm
defines. Two things still do not go through it.

The static runtime libraries: LTO code generation emits calls to library
functions such as fetestexcept and _dsign, and lld cannot take a bitcode
archive member for them after code generation has run. Compile them without LTO.

wow64 calls two functions from module level asm. Asm can only name a symbol the
linker knows, so they cannot be static.

